  <prompt>
    Author the single unified byte-author (D5). Create a NEW file
    `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs` implementing
    `(retained bytes, operation log) -&gt; patched bytes`: for each operation, resolve the target node
    by its `w14:paraId` (O(1), via `ParaIdPreParser`/`ExtractParaIds`), split the run at the
    run-local-offset PRESERVING `RunProperties`, and emit native `w:ins`/`w:del`/`w:comment`. Package
    parts never opened are copied verbatim; untouched subtrees within `document.xml` stay
    byte-identical. You MUST mutate the OpenXml DOM — NEVER string-edit `document.xml`. Migrate the
    EDGE-1…4 wisdom out of `DocxAnnotationWriter.cs` (comment-before-trackchange ordering; `w:delText`
    not `w:t` on deletes; monotonic revision-id seeding) into this engine BEFORE task 032 retires that
    class. Use the patch engine chosen by the task 005 A/B (Docxodus OR build-on-OpenXML-SDK) — read the
    task 005 decision record and follow it; do NOT re-litigate the A/B here. The engine is a STATELESS
    concrete singleton (ADR-010), `byte[]`-in/`byte[]`-out (ADR-007), and injects NO AI internals
    (ADR-013 Tier-1 NetArchTest). This task is GATED on task 006 (Phase 0 gate) being green.
    Do NOT implement the structural paragraph ops here — those are task 031, sequenced last.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET 8 developer fluent in the Open XML SDK (WordprocessingDocument, run/RunProperties
    cloning, InsertedRun/DeletedRun, CommentRangeStart/End) and OOXML tracked-change semantics. Owns
    the one place in R4 that writes `.docx` bytes and understands that correctness here (offset→run
    split over formatted/split runs and pre-existing tracked changes) is what makes the whole shadow
    architecture succeed.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A new `ComposeShadowPatchEngine` that applies an ID-anchored operation log surgically onto retained
    OOXML: every text edit / redline / comment lands at the intended `w14:paraId` + run-local-offset
    with ZERO write-path text-search; untouched package parts are verbatim and untouched `document.xml`
    subtrees are byte-identical; the EDGE-1…4 native-OOXML wisdom is carried over from
    `DocxAnnotationWriter`; an operation whose `paraId` cannot be resolved is refused, never applied to
    the wrong node.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §5.0 (the bridge = the real work; offset→run mapping is the hard piece), §5 Patch (backend)
      diagram, §3 invariants I-1/I-3/I-4/I-5/I-7, D5 (one byte-author). Spec FR-04, NFR-01, NFR-02,
      NFR-05. The current save uses two independent writers — `DocxAnnotationWriter` (text-search, the
      422 root cause) and `ComposeParagraphRedlineSynthesizer` (paragraph-diff). R4 consolidates both
      into this one operational engine. The operation schema (task 003) is the contract this engine
      consumes; the applier spike (task 005) proved the split-run + `w:ins`/`w:del` recipe on the CIPO
      doc and chose the underlying engine. Prior art (`notes/bridge-prior-art.md` finding #6): match
      `w:p` by `w14:paraId` → walk runs accumulating text length until the offset lands in run R →
      `Run.Clone()` split R preserving `RunProperties` → wrap inserts in `InsertedRun` / deletes in
      `DeletedRun` with Author/Date/Id → mutate the DOM, never string-edit.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs — the unified byte-author: resolve-by-paraId, split-run-at-offset, emit native w:ins/w:del/w:comment; stateless concrete singleton</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationWriter.cs — EDGE-1…4 native-OOXML wisdom to MIGRATE (comment-before-trackchange ordering; w:delText not w:t; monotonic revision-id seeding); LocateTarget (:316-369) is NOT migrated (text-search, killed)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeParagraphRedlineSynthesizer.cs — the paragraph-diff redline shape being consolidated into operational apply</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ParaIdPreParser.cs — document-order paraId extraction (incl. table cells/nested tables) reused to resolve nodes O(1)</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ — task 003 operation-schema contract (the op log this engine consumes) + task 005 applier-spike decision record (which engine won the A/B)</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/design.md §5.0, §5 (Patch backend), §3, D5</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/spec.md FR-04, NFR-01, NFR-02, NFR-05</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="003" status="pending">Operation schema — the shared versioned contract this engine consumes (op types + `{paraId, runIndex, offset|range}` anchor).</dependency>
      <dependency task="005" status="pending">Applier spike on the CIPO doc + patch-engine A/B — proves the split-run recipe and SELECTS the underlying engine (Docxodus vs OpenXML-SDK). This task follows that decision.</dependency>
      <dependency task="006" status="pending">Phase 0 GATE — HARD prerequisite; must be green before this engine is built into the write path.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-04">The engine MUST resolve each node by `w14:paraId` (O(1)) and split runs at the run-local-offset preserving `RunProperties`; MUST emit native `w:ins`/`w:del`/`w:comment`; MUST NOT text-search anywhere in the write path (invariant I-7).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec / NFR-01">Untouched package parts MUST be copied verbatim; untouched `document.xml` subtrees MUST be structurally faithful (byte-identical on untouched parts, XML-splice hardening option deferred to corpus results). MUST mutate the OpenXml DOM, NEVER string-edit `document.xml`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">`byte[]`-in / `byte[]`-out. No `Microsoft.Graph` type in the engine; the SPE hop stays in the endpoint/facade layer above `SpeFileStore`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-05">`Services/Compose/` injects NO AI internals (`IOpenAiClient`/executor/routing types); consume `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` only if AI capability is needed; Tier-1 NetArchTest MUST stay green.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">The engine is a STATELESS concrete singleton — no per-request state, no interface-for-one-impl ceremony.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / EDGE-migration">Migrate the EDGE-1…4 wisdom (comment-before-trackchange ordering; `w:delText` not `w:t`; monotonic revision-id seeding) from `DocxAnnotationWriter.cs` into this engine BEFORE task 032 deletes that class. Do NOT migrate `LocateTarget` (text-search — killed).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / §10 Placement Justification">State the Placement Justification in the PR (patch/byte authoring stays in `Services/Compose/`; reuses `ParaIdPreParser`/SPE seams) and cite `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`. Run `/conflict-check` before the PR — `Services/Compose/` overlaps r1/r2/r3 + ai-architecture-redesign-r2.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029 / CLAUDE.md §10">Measure BFF publish size; report absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (incl. PDBs), ≤60 MB ceiling. If Docxodus was adopted by task 005, verify its size delta here. Verify no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 / NFR-06">Through-the-wire seam proof is required for this write-path surface (authored in task 034); unit-green ≠ done. NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, or ctor-null tests.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Open XML SDK surgical patch (split-run preserving RunProperties, InsertedRun/DeletedRun, comment ranges); resolve-by-paraId O(1); EDGE-1…4 tracked-change ordering; DI minimalism; BFF hygiene</topic>
