  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the FULL rigor-level declaration (🔒 RIGOR / 📋 REASON / 📖 PROTOCOL STEPS). Confirm task 006 (Phase 0 gate) is GREEN — this task is gated. Read the task 003 op-schema contract + the task 005 A/B decision record (which underlying engine won). Load knowledge files + `bff-extensions.md`; state the Placement Justification for the PR.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Node resolution by paraId">Build the O(1) resolve-by-`w14:paraId` path reusing `ParaIdPreParser`/`ExtractParaIds` (incl. table cells / nested tables). An operation whose paraId does not resolve is REFUSED (surface a clear failure), never applied to a neighbouring node.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Split-run-at-offset (the hard piece)">Implement offset→run mapping: walk the target paragraph's runs accumulating text length until the run-local-offset lands in run R; `Run.Clone()`-split R preserving `RunProperties`; handle formatted/split runs and pre-existing tracked changes. This is the escalation-boundary edge (see &lt;escalation&gt;).</step>
    <step order="3" name="Emit native w:ins/w:del/w:comment + migrate EDGE-1…4">Wrap inserts in `InsertedRun`(w:ins), deletes in `DeletedRun`(w:del) with Author/Date/Id and `w:delText`; emit `w:comment` + comment ranges. Migrate the EDGE-1…4 wisdom (comment-before-trackchange ordering; `w:delText` not `w:t`; monotonic revision-id seeding) from `DocxAnnotationWriter`. Mutate the DOM — never string-edit `document.xml`.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Register + build">Register the engine as a stateless concrete singleton (ADR-010). Build the BFF; run the Tier-1 NetArchTest facade check; run existing `Services/Compose` unit tests (no regression). Add focused unit tests under `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/` (the through-the-wire seam proof is task 034).</step>
    <step order="5" name="Size/CVE + index + deviations">Publish; report absolute size + delta vs ~49.63 MB (incl. PDBs), ≤60 MB; `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` (no new HIGH CVE). Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅. Document any deviation in `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>`DocxAnnotationWriter` (text-search write path) + `ComposeParagraphRedlineSynthesizer` (paragraph-diff) — both slated for retirement (task 032).</existing>
    <extension>No — this REPLACES both and consolidates them into one byte-author (D5); the two-path split is exactly the defect being removed, so an "extend one of them" answer would keep the drift alive.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The text-search 422 class (interior-location edits fail with "a tracked change could not be located") and the two-independent-writer drift persist; structural edits remain impossible.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs (new — resolve-by-paraId, split-run, native w:ins/w:del/w:comment; EDGE-1…4 migrated)</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ (DI registration of the engine as a stateless concrete singleton)</output>
