  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">An interior text edit / redline / comment lands at the intended `w14:paraId` + run-local-offset with ZERO write-path text-search (code audit + unit tests confirm no text-search).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A corpus no-op save is byte-identical on untouched parts (package parts never opened are verbatim; untouched `document.xml` subtrees structurally faithful).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The run split preserves `RunProperties` across formatted/split runs and pre-existing tracked changes; native `w:ins`/`w:del` (with `w:delText`) and `w:comment` are emitted per EDGE-1…4 ordering.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: an operation with an unknown/unresolvable `paraId` is REFUSED (clear failure), never applied to the wrong node.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The engine is a stateless concrete singleton (ADR-010), `byte[]`-in/`byte[]`-out (ADR-007); `Services/Compose/` injects no AI-internal type (Tier-1 NetArchTest green).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The EDGE-1…4 wisdom is verifiably migrated (present in this engine) BEFORE task 032 deletes `DocxAnnotationWriter`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size reported absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline, ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE; BFF build + NetArchTest green; `/conflict-check` run before the PR.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The offset→run split over formatted/split runs AND pre-existing tracked changes cannot be made deterministic for a corpus case (e.g. an offset that falls inside an existing `w:ins`/`w:del` region, or a run boundary that Word will re-normalize). STOP and surface per root §6 / §6.5 rather than guessing a split that could mis-place bytes.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <notes>
    Front-loaded hard surface (design §6). Structural paragraph ops are NOT in this task — they are 031, sequenced last in the applier. The underlying engine (Docxodus vs OpenXML-SDK) is fixed by the task 005 A/B — follow that decision record, do not re-run the A/B here.

    --- COMPLETION (2026-07-22) ---
    DELIVERED: NEW `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs` (concrete stateless singleton) — `Apply(byte[] retained, ComposeOperationLog, comments?, author?, timestamp?) -> byte[]`. Promoted + hardened the task-005 `SpikeOpenXmlApplier`: O(1) resolve-by-w14:paraId (dictionary, ZERO write-path text-search — grep-verified), editor-visible run-flatten (MIRRORS `ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder.CollectRunBoundaries` — descends w:hyperlink/w:ins/w:del/w:sdt, atoms as single slots — NOT raw Elements&lt;Run&gt;(), per finding #2), general SplitRun preserving RunProperties on both halves (multi-child text+glyph), native w:ins/w:del(w:delText, EDGE-4)/w:comment. Migrated EDGE-1..4 (comment-before-trackchange ordering; w:delText; monotonic revision-id seeding) from DocxAnnotationWriter (NOT deleted — task 032). Sequential per-op application, re-flatten per op (finding #1 drift-safe). Added durable paraId+range-anchored `ComposeAnchoredComment` (text-search-free replacement for DocxAnnotation comments) + structured `ComposePatchException`/`ComposePatchErrorKind`.
    SCOPE HELD: text/mark/comment ops (insertText, deleteRange, replaceRange, setMark, clearMark) + comments. Structural ops (split/merge/insert/deleteParagraph) + setBlockAttr route to a clear task-031 NotSupported seam (ComposePatchErrorKind.StructuralOpNotYetImplemented). NOT routed through ComposeService.SaveAsync (task 032).
    ESCALATION EDGE (POML &lt;escalation&gt;, root §6.5): reconciling a new edit onto a run INSIDE a pre-existing w:ins/w:del is genuinely ambiguous — the engine REFUSES (TrackedChangeReconciliationUnsupported), deterministic, never mis-places bytes. Not a task blocker: corpus (CIPO) is track-changes-clean so the settled-run path is fully corpus-proven; the reconciliation semantic is surfaced for a later decision, not silently approximated.
    DI: `services.AddSingleton&lt;ComposeShadowPatchEngine&gt;()` in ComposeModule.cs (unconditional/symmetric per bff-extensions.md §F.1).
    TESTS: 15 unit tests `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/ComposeShadowPatchEngineTests.cs` (interior insert/delete/replace/setMark/comment land at paraId+offset; RunProperties preserved; flatten-over-hyperlink alignment; NEGATIVE unknown-paraId refused; no-op byte-identical; structural-op + tracked-change-reconciliation + bad-schema refused) + seam `tests/integration/seam/Compose/ComposeShadowPatchEngineByteDiffSeamTests.cs` (drives engine over EVERY corpus doc: no-op whole-file byte-identical + real interior insert leaves untouched PARTS byte-identical & untouched paragraph subtrees unchanged, reusing task-004 ComposeOoxmlPackagePartComparer).
    VERIFY: `dotnet build` GREEN; `dotnet test --filter ~Compose` = 541 passed / 0 failed; ADR013_ComposeFacadeTests (Tier-1) GREEN. (3 pre-existing ArchTest failures — ADR-007 Communication/Office, ADR-010 IComposeService/AutoFileSettings — are baseline, unrelated; my engine adds no new violation.)
    SIZE/CVE: compressed publish 47.48 MB incl PDBs / 46.66 MB excl (&lt;60 MB ceiling; below ~49.63 baseline; marginal delta ~0 — zero new package). No new HIGH CVE (System.Security.Cryptography.Xml HIGH is pre-existing transitive; engine adds no crypto/package).
    GATES: code-review PASS, adr-check PASS. /conflict-check: silent pass (no open PR on Services/Compose or ComposeModule.cs).
  </notes>

